  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of cross-border reconciliation between peoples living in Goma (DR Congo) and Nyundo (Rwand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to the reduction of inter-communal tensions between cross-border communities living in Goma and Nyundo dioceses, Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC).

The priests of two neighbouring dioceses of Goma and Nyundo, some representative authorities from Masisi and Rutshuru, community leaders and members of civil society in these territories will be trained and empowered to contribute to the peaceful coexistence on this sub region. The project plans to hold two peace festivals in the parishes of Goma and Rutshuru where inter-communal tensions are more acute in this period. Festivals will be organized around the theme &quot;Singing for peace and peaceful coexistence of ethnic communities.&quot;

In addition to workshops and sessions, CDJP Goma plans to organize radio and television broadcasts that will be produced with a strong participation of the authorities, youth and women in order to give a strong message of peace and coexistence to the cross-border communities.</narrative>
  </description>
